Task: JS tour-state store

Summary: source/tours/state.js holds the per-user completion map: seeded from
localized data (initTourState), read via hasCompleted, written optimistically
by markCompleted which persists the full map through core POST /wp/v2/users/me
(failures swallowed — worst case the tour re-auto-starts elsewhere).
launchTour always shows a tour and marks it completed on finish/dismiss;
autoStartTour gates on hasCompleted and never marks when nothing was shown
(startTour false). TOURS_META_KEY mirrors BVM\Tours::META_KEY.

Files:
- source/tours/state.js (new)
- tests/js/tours/state.test.js (new, 11 tests — TDD red confirmed first)

Why: FR-5 — auto-start-once gating + always-relaunchable tours, shared by all
three tour surfaces.

